"k": "Clinical guideline",
"g": "",
"t": "surgery",
"pop": "University of California, San Francisco, guidance for primary care clinicians.",
"f": "Phalloplasty usually happens in several stages; an erectile implant is typically placed roughly 9 months after the penis is created. Donor sites can bring scarring, wound breakdown, pain and reduced sensation or movement. Urethral narrowing typically appears 6 to 12 months after surgery. Review every 3 months in the first year is suggested.",
